1788685772 H:B9 K8 branchy honest kernel (D14 item 5) -- a genuinely data-dependent branch at ~50% mispredict (bit=(x>>60)&1 of an LCG stream, arms acc+x vs acc-i, 2M branches/run) still lands bebop inside ~2-3x of LLVM's csel choice | DID:added bench630/k8ht.bp + kernels/k8h.bp + rust_once/k8h.rs, wired honest.sh + perf.py (k8h_ms/k8h_loopwords), ran honest.sh R=11 and perf.py run --r 3, objdumped both binaries | GOT:bebop compiles the if to a real b.ne (40-word inner loop, b.cond count 2), rustc picks csel (csel x17,x15,x14,eq, no data branch); ratio 4.5x (honest.sh R=11) and 5.7x (a second R=11 run), k8h_loopwords=40 confirmed as K8's own inner while via objdump (min-loop extractor correctly beat the 101-word prelude trampoline loop), acc parity bit-exact (-7706214503032352720) for seed=1, perf.py run 0 alerts, roadmap_check GREEN | VERDICT:refuted
1788685932 H:K8 control -- how much of K8's 4.5-5.7x is the mispredict itself vs the stack-machine loop | DID:same k8ht.bp with bit = (i >> 4) & 1 (period-32 pattern, predicted) compiled by the same bebop.bin a903d33b, 5 interleaved runs pinned core 4 (box had the B5 agent's chain in flight, ps 25) | GOT:K8 total ms 28 33 34 37 38 (median 0.34 ms/rep), K8p 13 13 15 19 26 (median 0.15 ms/rep): the coin-flip branch costs ~0.19 ms/rep = ~9.5 ns per iteration, ~55 % of K8; K8p is still ~2.2x Rust's 0.069 ms (the 40-word loop, IR-rung territory) | VERDICT:confirmed -- T52 proceeds, as a tag-level csel in the IR rung (arms = REG/SYM/CONST tags), not a stream peephole
1788690078 H:B5 (research §2, D14 item 1) loop rotation to a bottom test -- [b->test][body_start:body][test:cond][pop 0][b.<inv cond>->body_start][endl] replaces the top-test [cond][b.cond->endl][body][b loop_start][endl] -- cuts the steady-state branch count from 2/iter to 1/iter; expected -1 loopword per loop, census b down, bcond unchanged, bin_words down | DID:emit_while_stmt + skip_while_cond (bracket-depth-0 scanner from pcond to body's `{`, skipping string/char literals) + skip_char_lit in bebop.bp; exit branch inverted via cond^1 (words derived by as+objdump into words.objdump, 335544320 forward b placeholder + 16777216 backward b.cond compensation word, 70/70 verified); tools/chain.sh bebop.bp --codegen (fixpoint gen3==gen4), then closed out: bebop.bin promoted gen4->bebop.bin (cp-to-temp+mv; the working bebop.bin was still a903d33b/B2, NOT yet promoted despite the handoff note -- root cause of the first invariants --freeze passing vacuously against the stale binary), census_allow.txt +1 line (bebop bcond 1629, B5 reason), invariants --freeze (re-run against the real f7a25d38), tools/battery.sh, tools/perf.py run --base a903d33b | GOT:fixpoint gen3==gen4 f7a25d38, battery GREEN (99/99 std, 52/52 construct parity, 17/17 diag, 13/13+1skip parity, 5/5 pool, ABI ok, invariants GREEN, words PASS 1 literal verified); bin_words 67775->68229 (ROSE +454, not fell); loopwords k1h 11->10, k3h 25->24, k4 15->14 (-1 as predicted), k2h 51->51 (unchanged, not -1); census bebop bcond 1610->1629 (+19, ALLOWed), b 1353->1371 (+18, ROSE not fell), cbz 120 unchanged, bl 1299->1303, ret 202->204 | VERDICT:refuted -- the per-loop steady-state win (-1 loopword on 3/4 kernels) landed, but the predicted global effects (b down, bcond unchanged, bin_words down) all went the other way: the forward `b->test` guard + duplicated bottom test that loop rotation adds costs more static words across bebop.bp's ~200 while sites than the removed per-iteration branch saves; k2h's loop was already at its floor from B1
