1788950951 H:F2 cannot land because the exit-code space is not partitioned -- vs_mask_take/free and vs_cs_take/free exit sys_exit(99/100/119/120 + site) for site 1..20, so the compiler can emit ANY code in 99..140 -- and T122's reserved table is short of the builtins the compiler actually dispatches | DID:worker added selfcheck_exit(kind, site) modelled on cap_exit -- ONE code, 201, with `compiler self-check <kind>.<site>` on stderr -- and routed all 18 self-check sites through it: the four base+site families, the four fntab[4548] boundary checks that aliased 102, the four cs-mask checks that aliased 104 and used the undocumented 105/106, and the two diag_exit 103/107 register-model invariants; appended the seven missing hashes to rsv3 in the SIGNED spelling that table uses; added neg/c113_shadowclz and neg/c114_shadowwait4. Main session rebased the patch onto A6 step 2B -- the lane cut its tree at 5be7adf, BEFORE 2B, so applying its file wholesale silently REVERTED 2B, which the words gate caught by flagging the stp/ldp x15,x14 pair and cbnz .+20 as new literals | GOT:fixpoint gen3 == gen4 == 045d0380 on the rebased tree; battery GREEN, constructs 89/0, std_golden 114/0, invariants GREEN, words PASS; census 42330 1194 124 0 917 1885 296. The census delta is MEASURED by a four-arm sweep, not argued -- baseline / partition only / the seven hashes only / both -- and the arms are exactly additive with the ENTIRE branch delta belonging to the partition arm, so the reserved table costs ZERO branches; rebased onto 2B the same change reads 1190 -> 1194 where the lane measured 1191 -> 1195, the same +4. Verified independently after the merge: the only literal in sys_exit() is 201, diag_exit uses only 99, 100, 101, 102, 104 in that range each with one meaning, zero base+site families remain, so 103, 105, 106 and 107 are FREE for F2. Behavioural probe: all seven of clz/crc32/crc32x/sys_msync/sys_run/sys_setaffinity/sys_wait4 now give rc=99 `reserved word used as a fn name`, `